SEC. 70001. REFERENCES TO THE INTERNAL REVENUE CODE OF 1986, ETC.
This section establishes that any amendments or repeals in this title refer to the Internal Revenue Code of 1986. It also specifies that the general rule for the effect of rate changes (Section 15 of the Code) will not apply to any tax rate changes made by this title.

SEC. 70101. EXTENSION AND ENHANCEMENT OF REDUCED RATES.
This section makes the individual income tax rate brackets from the 2017 tax law permanent, removing the expiration date of January 1, 2026. It also modifies the inflation adjustment calculation for the rate brackets, using a different base year for determining the thresholds for the 12% and 22% brackets. The changes apply to taxable years beginning after December 31, 2025.

SEC. 70102. EXTENSION AND ENHANCEMENT OF INCREASED STANDARD DEDUCTION.
This section makes the increased standard deduction amounts permanent. It further increases the standard deduction to $23,625 for joint filers and $15,750 for single filers, with these amounts indexed for inflation. The changes apply to taxable years beginning after December 31, 2024.

SEC. 70103. TERMINATION OF DEDUCTION FOR PERSONAL EXEMPTIONS OTHER THAN TEMPORARY SENIOR DEDUCTION.
This section makes the suspension of the personal exemption deduction permanent. It creates a new temporary deduction of $6,000 for taxpayers aged 65 or older, which is reduced by 6% of modified adjusted gross income over $75,000 ($150,000 for joint filers). This senior deduction is available for taxable years beginning before January 1, 2029, and requires a valid Social Security number.

SEC. 70104. EXTENSION AND ENHANCEMENT OF INCREASED CHILD TAX CREDIT.
This section makes the $2,000 Child Tax Credit permanent and increases the credit amount to $2,200. It also makes the $1,400 refundable portion of the credit permanent and subject to inflation adjustments. The section requires taxpayers and qualifying children to have valid Social Security numbers to claim the credit.

SEC. 70105. EXTENSION AND ENHANCEMENT OF DEDUCTION FOR QUALIFIED BUSINESS INCOME.
This section makes the 20% deduction for qualified business income (QBI) permanent. It increases the taxable income thresholds for the phase-in of the limitation on this deduction to $75,000 for single filers and $150,000 for joint filers. It also establishes a minimum deduction of $400 for taxpayers with at least $1,000 of active qualified business income.

SEC. 70106. EXTENSION AND ENHANCEMENT OF INCREASED ESTATE AND GIFT TAX EXEMPTION AMOUNTS.
This section makes the increased estate and gift tax exemption amount permanent and raises it to $15,000,000, indexed for inflation. The previous scheduled reduction of the exemption to $5,000,000 is repealed. The changes apply to estates of decedents dying and gifts made after December 31, 2025.

SEC. 70107. EXTENSION OF INCREASED ALTERNATIVE MINIMUM TAX EXEMPTION AMOUNTS AND MODIFICATION OF PHASEOUT THRESHOLDS.
This section makes the increased Alternative Minimum Tax (AMT) exemption amounts permanent. It modifies the inflation adjustment for the exemption amounts and changes the phaseout threshold for the $1,000,000 exemption amount. The phaseout for this higher exemption amount is now reduced by 50% of the income over the threshold, instead of 25%.

SEC. 70108. EXTENSION AND MODIFICATION OF LIMITATION ON DEDUCTION FOR QUALIFIED RESIDENCE INTEREST.
This section makes the $750,000 limit on the deduction for qualified residence interest permanent. It also treats mortgage insurance premiums as deductible interest, effectively making the deduction for these premiums permanent. The changes apply to taxable years beginning after December 31, 2025.

SEC. 70109. EXTENSION AND MODIFICATION OF LIMITATION ON CASUALTY LOSS DEDUCTION.
This section makes the limitation on the casualty loss deduction permanent, which only allows the deduction for losses from federally declared disasters. It expands the definition to include "State declared disasters" as determined by a Governor and the Secretary of the Treasury. The changes apply to taxable years beginning after December 31, 2025.

SEC. 70110. TERMINATION OF MISCELLANEOUS ITEMIZED DEDUCTIONS OTHER THAN EDUCATOR EXPENSES.
This section makes the suspension of miscellaneous itemized deductions subject to the 2% floor permanent. It creates a new deduction for educator expenses, which is not subject to the 2% floor, and expands the definition to include coaches and certain nonathletic instructional equipment. The changes apply to taxable years beginning after December 31, 2025.

SEC. 70111. LIMITATION ON TAX BENEFIT OF ITEMIZED DEDUCTIONS.
This section reinstates the Pease limitation on itemized deductions, reducing them by 2/37 of the amount by which a taxpayer's income exceeds the threshold for the 37% tax bracket. This limitation is applied after all other limitations on itemized deductions. The changes apply to taxable years beginning after December 31, 2025.

SEC. 70112. EXTENSION AND MODIFICATION OF QUALIFIED TRANSPORTATION FRINGE BENEFITS.
This section makes the exclusion for qualified transportation fringe benefits permanent. It repeals the exclusion for qualified bicycle commuting reimbursements, making them taxable. The changes apply to taxable years beginning after December 31, 2025.

SEC. 70113. EXTENSION AND MODIFICATION OF LIMITATION ON DEDUCTION AND EXCLUSION FOR MOVING EXPENSES.
This section makes the suspension of the deduction and exclusion for moving expenses permanent. It creates an exception for members of the intelligence community, allowing them to deduct moving expenses and exclude employer reimbursements. The changes apply to taxable years beginning after December 31, 2025.

SEC. 70114. EXTENSION AND MODIFICATION OF LIMITATION ON WAGERING LOSSES.
This section modifies the deduction for wagering losses, allowing a deduction equal to 90% of the losses, but only to the extent of wagering gains. The definition of wagering losses is expanded to include any deductions incurred in carrying on a wagering transaction. The changes apply to taxable years beginning after December 31, 2025.

SEC. 70115. EXTENSION AND ENHANCEMENT OF INCREASED LIMITATION ON CONTRIBUTIONS TO ABLE ACCOUNTS.
This section makes the increased contribution limit to ABLE accounts permanent. It modifies the inflation adjustment for the contribution limit, using a different base year. The changes apply to contributions made after December 31, 2025.

SEC. 70116. EXTENSION AND ENHANCEMENT OF SAVERS CREDIT ALLOWED FOR ABLE CONTRIBUTIONS.
This section makes the Savers Credit permanent for contributions to ABLE accounts. It increases the maximum credit amount from $2,000 to $2,100. The changes apply to taxable years ending after December 31, 2025.

SEC. 70117. EXTENSION OF ROLLOVERS FROM QUALIFIED TUITION PROGRAMS TO ABLE ACCOUNTS PERMITTED.
This section makes permanent the ability to roll over funds from a qualified tuition program (529 plan) to an ABLE account. The changes apply to taxable years beginning after December 31, 2025.

SEC. 70118. EXTENSION OF TREATMENT OF CERTAIN INDIVIDUALS PERFORMING SERVICES IN THE SINAI PENINSULA AND ENHANCEMENT TO INCLUDE ADDITIONAL AREAS.
This section makes permanent the special tax treatment for members of the Armed Forces serving in the Sinai Peninsula. It expands the definition of "qualified hazardous duty area" to include Kenya, Mali, Burkina Faso, and Chad. The changes take effect on January 1, 2026.

SEC. 70119. EXTENSION AND MODIFICATION OF EXCLUSION FROM GROSS INCOME OF STUDENT LOANS DISCHARGED ON ACCOUNT OF DEATH OR DISABILITY.
This section makes permanent the exclusion from gross income for student loans discharged due to the death or total and permanent disability of the student. It expands the definition of loans covered to include private education loans. The exclusion requires the taxpayer to include their Social Security number on their tax return.

SEC. 70120. LIMITATION ON INDIVIDUAL DEDUCTIONS FOR CERTAIN STATE AND LOCAL TAXES, ETC.
This section makes the $10,000 limit on the deduction for state and local taxes (SALT) permanent. It increases the limit to $40,000 for 2025, with annual increases of 1% through 2029, before reverting to $10,000. The increased limit is phased down by 30% of the amount by which a taxpayer's modified adjusted gross income exceeds $500,000.

SEC. 70201. NO TAX ON TIPS.
This section creates a new deduction for qualified tips received by an individual, up to a maximum of $25,000 per year. The deduction is phased out for taxpayers with modified adjusted gross income over $150,000 ($300,000 for joint filers). The deduction is temporary, applying to taxable years beginning after December 31, 2024, and before January 1, 2029.

SEC. 70202. NO TAX ON OVERTIME.
This section creates a new deduction for qualified overtime compensation, up to a maximum of $12,500 for single filers and $25,000 for joint filers. The deduction is phased out for taxpayers with modified adjusted gross income over $150,000 ($300,000 for joint filers). The deduction is temporary, applying to taxable years beginning after December 31, 2024, and before January 1, 2029.

SEC. 70203. NO TAX ON CAR LOAN INTEREST.
This section creates a new deduction for interest paid on loans for the purchase of a new passenger vehicle, up to a maximum of $10,000 per year. The deduction is phased out for taxpayers with modified adjusted gross income over $100,000 ($200,000 for joint filers). The deduction is temporary, applying to taxable years beginning after December 31, 2024, and before January 1, 2029.

SEC. 70204. TRUMP ACCOUNTS AND CONTRIBUTION PILOT PROGRAM.
This section creates a new type of tax-advantaged savings account called a "Trump Account" for individuals under 18. Contributions are limited to $5,000 per year, and the funds must be invested in specific low-cost index funds. The section also creates a pilot program providing a $1,000 contribution to a Trump Account for eligible children born between 2025 and 2028.

SEC. 70301. FULL EXPENSING FOR CERTAIN BUSINESS PROPERTY.
This section makes the 100% bonus depreciation deduction for qualified property permanent. It also makes the 100% expensing for certain plants bearing fruits and nuts permanent. The changes apply to property acquired after January 19, 2025.

SEC. 70302. FULL EXPENSING OF DOMESTIC RESEARCH AND EXPERIMENTAL EXPENDITURES.
This section allows taxpayers to deduct domestic research and experimental expenditures immediately, rather than amortizing them over 5 years. It also allows for an election to amortize these expenditures over a period of not less than 60 months. The changes apply to amounts paid or incurred in taxable years beginning after December 31, 2024.

SEC. 70303. MODIFICATION OF LIMITATION ON BUSINESS INTEREST.
This section makes the special rule for the business interest limitation for small businesses permanent. It expands the definition of "floor plan financing" to include certain trailers and campers. The changes apply to taxable years beginning after December 31, 2024.

SEC. 70304. EXTENSION AND ENHANCEMENT OF PAID FAMILY AND MEDICAL LEAVE CREDIT.
This section makes the paid family and medical leave credit permanent. It allows employers to claim the credit based on either wages paid to employees on leave or premiums paid for an insurance policy providing such leave. The changes apply to taxable years beginning after December 31, 2025.

SEC. 70305. EXCEPTIONS FROM LIMITATIONS ON DEDUCTION FOR BUSINESS MEALS.
This section creates an exception to the general denial of the deduction for business meals for expenses described in specific sections. It also exempts meals provided on certain fishing boats and at certain fish processing facilities from the 50% deduction limitation. The changes apply to amounts paid or incurred after December 31, 2025.

SEC. 70306. INCREASED DOLLAR LIMITATIONS FOR EXPENSING OF CERTAIN DEPRECIABLE BUSINESS ASSETS.
This section increases the maximum amount that can be expensed under Section 179 from $1,000,000 to $2,500,000. It also increases the phase-out threshold for this deduction from $2,500,000 to $4,000,000. The changes apply to property placed in service in taxable years beginning after December 31, 2024.

SEC. 70307. SPECIAL DEPRECIATION ALLOWANCE FOR QUALIFIED PRODUCTION PROPERTY.
This section creates a new 100% special depreciation allowance for qualified production property, which is a portion of nonresidential real property used in manufacturing, production, or refining. The property must be placed in service before January 1, 2031, and the construction must begin after January 19, 2025. The allowance is subject to recapture if the property ceases to be used for a qualified production activity within 10 years.

SEC. 70308. ENHANCEMENT OF ADVANCED MANUFACTURING INVESTMENT CREDIT.
This section increases the advanced manufacturing investment credit from 25% to 35% of the qualified investment. The changes apply to property placed in service after December 31, 2025.

SEC. 70309. SPACEPORTS ARE TREATED LIKE AIRPORTS UNDER EXEMPT FACILITY BOND RULES.
This section expands the definition of exempt facility bonds to include spaceports. It defines a spaceport as a facility used for manufacturing, assembling, or repairing spacecraft, flight control operations, or providing launch and reentry services. The changes apply to obligations issued after the date of enactment.

SEC. 70311. MODIFICATIONS RELATED TO FOREIGN TAX CREDIT LIMITATION.
This section modifies the rules for allocating deductions to foreign source net CFC tested income for purposes of the foreign tax credit limitation. It requires that the deduction under Section 250(a)(1)(B) be allocated to this income, while interest and research expenses are not. The changes apply to taxable years beginning after December 31, 2025.

SEC. 70312. MODIFICATIONS TO DETERMINATION OF DEEMED PAID CREDIT FOR TAXES PROPERLY ATTRIBUTABLE TO TESTED INCOME.
This section increases the deemed paid foreign tax credit for tested income from 80% to 90%. It also disallows a foreign tax credit for 10% of foreign income taxes paid with respect to distributions of previously taxed net CFC tested income. The changes apply to taxable years beginning after December 31, 2025.

SEC. 70313. SOURCING CERTAIN INCOME FROM THE SALE OF INVENTORY PRODUCED IN THE UNITED STATES.
This section provides that income from the sale of inventory produced in the U.S. and sold through a foreign branch will be treated as foreign source income, but only up to 50% of the total income from the sale. The changes apply to taxable years beginning after December 31, 2025.

SEC. 70321. MODIFICATION OF DEDUCTION FOR FOREIGN-DERIVED DEDUCTION ELIGIBLE INCOME AND NET CFC TESTED INCOME.
This section reduces the deduction for foreign-derived deduction eligible income (FDDEI) from 37.5% to 33.34%. It also reduces the deduction for net CFC tested income from 50% to 40%. The changes apply to taxable years beginning after December 31, 2025.

SEC. 70322. DETERMINATION OF DEDUCTION ELIGIBLE INCOME.
This section expands the definition of foreign-derived deduction eligible income (FDDEI) to include income from the sale or disposition of intangible property and depreciable property. It also limits the expense apportionment for FDDEI to expenses that are properly allocable to the gross income. The changes apply to sales or dispositions occurring after June 16, 2025.

SEC. 70323. RULES RELATED TO DEEMED INTANGIBLE INCOME.
This section repeals the concept of "global intangible low-taxed income" (GILTI) and replaces it with "net CFC tested income." It eliminates the 10% deemed return on qualified business asset investment (QBAI) that reduced the GILTI inclusion. The changes apply to taxable years beginning after December 31, 2025.

SEC. 70331. EXTENSION AND MODIFICATION OF BASE EROSION MINIMUM TAX AMOUNT.
This section makes the Base Erosion Minimum Tax (BEAT) permanent and increases the rate from 10% to 10.5%. It also makes technical corrections to the provision. The changes apply to taxable years beginning after December 31, 2025.

SEC. 70341. COORDINATION OF BUSINESS INTEREST LIMITATION WITH INTEREST CAPITALIZATION PROVISIONS.
This section clarifies that the business interest limitation applies to business interest that would otherwise be capitalized. It requires that the allowed amount of business interest be applied first to capitalized interest, with the remainder applied to deductible interest. The changes apply to taxable years beginning after December 31, 2025.

SEC. 70342. DEFINITION OF ADJUSTED TAXABLE INCOME FOR BUSINESS INTEREST LIMITATION.
This section modifies the definition of adjusted taxable income for the business interest limitation. It adds amounts included in gross income under Sections 951(a), 951A(a), and 78 to the calculation. The changes apply to taxable years beginning after December 31, 2025.

SEC. 70351. PERMANENT EXTENSION OF LOOK-THRU RULE FOR RELATED CONTROLLED FOREIGN CORPORATIONS.
This section makes permanent the "look-thru" rule for related controlled foreign corporations (CFCs). This rule allows certain payments between related CFCs to be recharacterized as income that is not subject to Subpart F. The changes apply to taxable years of foreign corporations beginning after December 31, 2025.

SEC. 70352. REPEAL OF ELECTION FOR 1-MONTH DEFERRAL IN DETERMINATION OF TAXABLE YEAR OF SPECIFIED FOREIGN CORPORATIONS.
This section repeals the election that allowed specified foreign corporations to use a one-month deferral in determining their taxable year. The changes apply to taxable years of specified foreign corporations beginning after November 30, 2025.

SEC. 70353. RESTORATION OF LIMITATION ON DOWNWARD ATTRIBUTION OF STOCK OWNERSHIP IN APPLYING CONSTRUCTIVE OWNERSHIP RULES.
This section restores the limitation on downward attribution of stock ownership in the constructive ownership rules. It prevents a U.S. person from being considered as owning stock owned by a foreign person. It also creates a new category of "foreign controlled United States shareholders" and "foreign controlled foreign corporations" for Subpart F purposes.

SEC. 70354. MODIFICATIONS TO PRO RATA SHARE RULES.
This section modifies the rules for determining a U.S. shareholder's pro rata share of a controlled foreign corporation's (CFC) Subpart F income. The pro rata share is now based on the stock owned and the period during which the shareholder owned the stock and the corporation was a CFC. The changes apply to taxable years of foreign corporations beginning after December 31, 2025. [end of text]


